    <p>
      The first apportionment method we'll study is due to none other than Alexander Hamilton!
    </p>

    <definition>
      <title>Hamilton's Method</title>

      <p>
        Start by giving each state its lower quota.
        Then, in order of largest fractional part, distribute the remaining seats.
      </p>
    </definition>

    <exercise>
      <title>The winners are...</title>

      <statement>
        <p>
          Determine which professors get their upper quota of boxes of coffee thanks to Alexander Hamilton.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <answer>
        <p>
          The professors with fractional rank one through four.
          <table>
            <title>Hamilton Apportionment</title>

